{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f2251d7a-ed4b-4db1-b73f-a6a6b49e3dc9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-880cff82f5ac80c2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9006-td_hplvb/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9006-decomposition.md","content":"# Feature Store as a supported RHOAI component — Decomposition Summary\n\nParent strategy: RHAISTRAT-9006 (Feature Store as a supported RHOAI component, priority Major, status Refinement Done).\n\nThe strategy brings Feast in as a supported, installable RHOAI component. Feast is a\n**new component**: it has a reserved Jira component (`Feature Store`) but no productized\nrepository, no build pipeline, and no operator integration, and it has **no architecture\ncontext file** — so Rule 20 generates a full onboarding chain (`repo-onboarding` +\n`license-validation` parallel start → `konflux-onboarding` after repo → general\nimplementation after license-validation, parallel with konflux). Dashboard, Platform\nOperator, Notebooks, and Documentation are existing components.\n\nThe strategy carries one genuine unknown — which Feast deployment topology to productize\n(operator-based vs. standalone server per project). The answer changes what the Platform\nOperator integration and the Dashboard endpoint surfacing build against, so it becomes a\nblocking Investigation (E001) with two bounded conditional branches (E010 in each branch).\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E001 | Select the Feast deployment topology to productize | Investigation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E002 | Create midstream Feast repository under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E003 | License validation for Feast and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E004 | Konflux build pipeline onboarding for the Feast repository | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E005 | Productize the Feast server image and SDK package | Implementation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E006 | Enable Feature Store as a managed component in the Platform Operator | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E007 | Preinstall the Feast SDK in a supported workbench image | Implementation | RHOAI Notebooks | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E008 | Dashboard Feature Store enablement display and endpoint links | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E009 | Feature Store product documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E010 | Productize the Feast operator-based deployment | Implementation (branch A) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E010 | Productize the standalone per-project Feast server deployment | Implementation (branch B) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n\nMain-plan epics: E001–E009 (9). Branch epics BRANCH-A-E010 and BRANCH-B-E010 are\nconditional alternatives attached to the gating Investigation; they are not standalone\nJira issues and are excluded from the main-plan critical path.\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\nArrows point from dependency to dependent (\"X --> Y\" = X must complete before Y starts).\nDotted arrows are conditional branch edges.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n  E001[E001 Investigation: topology] --> E006[E006 Platform Operator enablement]\n  E001 --> E008[E008 Dashboard card + links]\n  E002[E002 repo-onboarding] --> E004[E004 konflux-onboarding]\n  E002 --> E005[E005 Feast image + SDK productization]\n  E003[E003 license-validation] --> E005\n  E003 --> E006\n  E003 --> E007[E007 Workbench SDK preinstall]\n  E005 --> E007\n  E006 --> E008\n  E002 --> E009[E009 docs]\n  E003 --> E009\n  E004 --> E009\n  E005 --> E009\n  E006 --> E009\n  E007 --> E009\n  E008 --> E009\n  E001 -.-> BRA[BRANCH-A-E010 operator-based deployment]\n  E002 -.-> BRA\n  E003 -.-> BRA\n  E001 -.-> BRB[BRANCH-B-E010 per-project server]\n  E002 -.-> BRB\n  E003 -.-> BRB\n```\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E002 → E004 | Rule 5 | Konflux pipeline needs the repository; always serial. |\n| E002 → E005 | Rule 6 | Image/SDK productization needs the onboarded repo's code. |\n| E003 → E005 | Rule 9 | If licenses fail, dependencies change and the productization approach changes. |\n| (none) E004 ⇢ E005 | Rule 10 | Konflux onboarding and general implementation run parallel — the coupling is enforced by the \"build pipeline green\" AC on E005 (Rule 25), never a DAG edge. |\n| E001 → E006 | Rule 3 | Topology decision rewrites the operator integration approach; true gate, `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite`. |\n| E003 → E006 | Rule 9 | Operator references productized Feast images; license outcome can change what is shippable. |\n| (none) E005 ⇢ E006 | Rule 13 | Pinned image digests consumed by the operator are configuration references — AC gate (\"pinned digest available\"), not a dependency edge. |\n| E003 → E007 | Rule 9 | Workbench image bundles the Feast SDK and its transitive deps; license outcome gates bundling. |\n| E005 → E007 | Rule 13 | The SDK package is a build-against library artifact the workbench image consumes. |\n| E001 → E008 | Rule 3 | Endpoint shape per project differs by topology (project-scoped servers vs. operator-managed); true gate, `rewrite`. |\n| E006 → E008 | Rule 13 | Dashboard builds against the enablement state surface the Platform Operator exposes (per architecture context, the Dashboard reads component CRs / per-component feature flags). |\n| E001 → BRANCH-*-E010 | Rule 3 | Branch epics exist only for the matching topology outcome; `gate_failure_impact.action=remove`. |\n| E002 → BRANCH-*-E010 | Rule 6 | Deployment productization builds from the onboarded repo. |\n| E003 → BRANCH-*-E010 | Rule 9 | License outcome can change what deployment artifacts are shippable. |\n| (none) E005 ⇢ BRANCH-*-E010 | Rule 13 | Server image digests referenced by deployment artifacts are configuration references — AC, not an edge. |\n| E002–E008 → E009 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by every main-plan Implementation epic; docs describe what was built. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n|-----|----------|-------|\n| HLR-1 — Admins can enable a supported Feature Store through the Platform Operator with productized images | P0 | E002, E003, E004, E005, E006, BRANCH-A-E010 / BRANCH-B-E010 (topology-selected) |\n| HLR-2 — Feast SDK preinstalled in at least one supported workbench image | P1 | E003, E005, E007 |\n| HLR-3 — Dashboard shows the Feature Store as enabled and links to its endpoints per project | P1 | E006 (enablement surface), E008 |\n| HLR-4 — Product documentation: enablement, getting-started, supported limits | P2 | E009 |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted Teams table,\n   no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no Non-Functional\n   Requirements. Epic acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs and problem\n   statement. Team assignments were inferred — Dashboard from its architecture context\n   (\"RHOAI Dashboard\"), the rest from component-ownership conventions (\"RHOAI Feature\n   Store\" is a new team for a new component and must be confirmed before planning).\n2. **Docs priority vs. HLR priority**: HLR-4 is P2, but the docs-authoring epic is P1 per\n   the mandatory docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter priority\n   `Major` → P1). This is by rule, not an oversight.\n3. **Scope trap guard**: managed offline-store infrastructure is explicitly out of scope\n   (customers bring their own storage). The Dashboard epic is link-out only (no\n   feature-authoring UI), and the docs epic must state supported limits including the\n   bring-your-own offline store — none of the epics may imply a managed offline store.\n4. **New component, no architecture context**: Feast has no architecture context file, so\n   architecture-context validation of the strategy's Feast claims is impossible; the\n   onboarding chain (Rule 20) stands in for that validation. `Feature Store` is used\n   verbatim from the canonical component list.\n5. **License risk**: Feast's transitive dependency tree is unvetted; license failure\n   would change dependencies across E005, E006, E007 and both branch epics — hence\n   license-validation is P0 and blocks all general implementations (Rule 9).\n\n## Conditional Decomposition Branches\n\nThe topology Investigation (E001) has two bounded outcomes:\n\n- **Branch A — operator-based deployment**: `RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E010.md` productizes\n  the Feast operator-based deployment (operator artifacts and lifecycle management) so\n  the Platform Operator manages Feature Store through the operator.\n- **Branch B — standalone server per project**: `RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E010.md`\n  productizes a project-scoped Feast server deployment with per-project endpoints and\n  customer-provided offline-store configuration.\n\nBoth branch files set `branch`, `gated_by=RHAISTRAT-9006-E001` (also in `dependencies`),\nand `gate_failure_impact.action=remove`. The Platform Operator epic (E006) and Dashboard\nepic (E008) exist in both outcomes and are therefore main-plan epics gated on E001 with\n`rewrite` impact rather than branch epics. No main-plan epic depends on a branch epic.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable. There is no external dependency with uncertain timing; the single open\nquestion is an internal topology decision handled by the Investigation and its\nconditional branches. All onboarding work (E002–E005) is topology-independent and\ndelivers risk-reduction value regardless of the outcome.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":37388,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87f4f14a8699c610","agent_id":"a2075be10e54066c2","session_id":"c063278f-b757-405a-ad7d-6ea1f816e2d2","uuid":"4b7fb1e6-6e80-40c5-a431-b7b436168a44","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:33:14.052Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9006"}
