ts of the productized Feast images —\n  no floating tags.\n- The enablement state is exposed consistently with other managed components,\n  in a form the Dashboard can read.\n- Pinned image digests for the productized Feast artifacts are available at\n  execution time (configuration gate, not a scheduling dependency).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): administrators enable the supported Feature Store through the\n  Platform Operator.\n- HLR-3 (P1): produces the enablement surface the Dashboard displays.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Scope is gated on the deployment topology investigation; if the selected\n  topology differs from the working assumption, this epic's reconciliation\n  approach is rewritten (the enablement capability itself remains).\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- The deployment topology to reconcile is resolved by the gating\n  investigation; no other open questions affect this epic's existence.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42329,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87f4f14a8699c610","agent_id":"a2075be10e54066c2","session_id":"c063278f-b757-405a-ad7d-6ea1f816e2d2","uuid":"8d26d578-ab9d-4968-b261-cbaa451674af","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:34:25.971Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9006"}
