{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8babdb564e890969","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n3\ttitle: Select the Feast deployment topology to productize\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: RHOAI Feature Store\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Select the Feast deployment topology to productize\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's open question: which Feast deployment\n30\ttopology RHOAI productizes first — the operator-based deployment or the standalone\n31\tserver per project. Upstream Feast supports both; their supportability\n32\tcharacteristics (lifecycle management, upgrade path, per-project isolation, resource\n33\tfootprint, alignment with how the Platform Operator manages other components)\n34\tdiffer. The outcome determines the shape of the Platform Operator integration and\n35\tthe Dashboard endpoint surfacing, and selects between the two conditional\n36\tdeployment-productization branches in this decomposition.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Define evaluation criteria for both topologies: lifecycle management (install,\n41\t  upgrade, rollback), per-project isolation, resource footprint, operational\n42\t  supportability, and alignment with the Platform Operator's managed-component model.\n43\t- Gather evidence: review upstream Feast documentation and source for both\n44\t  deployment modes, and exercise Feast locally (SDK and server) where possible to\n45\t  validate assumptions.\n46\t- Produce a decision record that names the selected topology with the\n47\t  supportability rationale, and records the consequences for the Platform Operator\n48\t  integration and the per-project endpoint model.\n49\t- Obtain stakeholder confirmation of the selection (product/support sign-off).\n50\t- Update the scope of the downstream gated work to match the selected outcome.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A decision record exists that names exactly one selected topology\n55\t  (operator-based or standalone per-project server).\n56\t- Both topologies are assessed against the defined evaluation criteria, with the\n57\t  evidence cited for each.\n58\t- The decision record states what the selection means for the Platform Operator\n59\t  integration scope and the per-project endpoint model used by the Dashboard.\n60\t- The selection has been reviewed and confirmed by the accountable stakeholders.\n61\t- The downstream gated epics' scopes have been reconciled with the selected\n62\t  outcome.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-1 (P0): gates the approach by which administrators enable the supported\n67\t  Feature Store through the Platform Operator.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-beb8482f0e050acf","agent_id":"a67a3ba4003051f8b","session_id":"c063278f-b757-405a-ad7d-6ea1f816e2d2","uuid":"b320146e-6d9b-4ecc-8495-86390c78fb49","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:38:35.773Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8babdb564e890969","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
