ss all downstream\n49\timplementations.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A scan report exists covering the Feast server and the Feast SDK dependency\n54\t  trees, including transitive dependencies.\n55\t- Every flagged license has a recorded disposition: approved exception,\n56\t  replacement dependency, or escalation with a recommendation.\n57\t- No unresolved license blockers remain for shipping the productized images or\n58\t  bundling the Feast SDK in a supported workbench image.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-1 (P0): productized images must be license-clean.\n63\t- HLR-2 (P1): the SDK bundled into workbench images must be license-clean.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-beb8482f0e050acf","agent_id":"a67a3ba4003051f8b","session_id":"c063278f-b757-405a-ad7d-6ea1f816e2d2","uuid":"4d564122-488f-4dc6-8649-b043e5de7c9b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:38:41.252Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-838a5a05c158f4e9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
