ore planning).\n117\t2. **Docs priority vs. HLR priority**: HLR-4 is P2, but the docs-authoring epic is P1 per\n118\t   the mandatory docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter priority\n119\t   `Major` → P1). This is by rule, not an oversight.\n120\t3. **Scope trap guard**: managed offline-store infrastructure is explicitly out of scope\n121\t   (customers bring their own storage). The Dashboard epic is link-out only (no\n122\t   feature-authoring UI), and the docs epic must state supported limits including the\n123\t   bring-your-own offline store — none of the epics may imply a managed offline store.\n124\t4. **New component, no architecture context**: Feast has no architecture context file, so\n125\t   architecture-context validation of the strategy's Feast claims is impossible; the\n126\t   onboarding chain (Rule 20) stands in for that validation. `Feature Store` is used\n127\t   verbatim from the canonical component list.\n128\t5. **License risk**: Feast's transitive dependency tree is unvetted; license failure\n129\t   would change dependencies across E005, E006, E007 and both branch epics — hence\n130\t   license-validation is P0 and blocks all general implementations (Rule 9).\n131\t\n132\t## Conditional Decomposition Branches\n133\t\n134\tThe topology Investigation (E001) has two bounded outcomes:\n135\t\n136\t- **Branch A — operator-based deployment**: `RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E010.md` productizes\n137\t  the Feast operator-based deployment (operator artifacts and lifecycle management) so\n138\t  the Platform Operator manages Feature Store through the operator.\n139\t- **Branch B — standalone server per project**: `RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E010.md`\n140\t  productizes a project-scoped Feast server deployment with per-project endpoints and\n141\t  customer-provided offline-store configuration.\n142\t\n143\tBoth branch files set `branch`, `gated_by=RHAISTRAT-9006-E001` (also in `dependencies`),\n144\tand `gate_failure_impact.action=remove`. The Platform Operator epic (E006) and Dashboard\n145\tepic (E008) exist in both outcomes and are therefore main-plan epics gated on E001 with\n146\t`rewrite` impact rather than branch epics. No main-plan epic depends on a branch epic.\n147\t\n148\t## Tiered Delivery\n149\t\n150\tNot applicable. There is no external dependency with uncertain timing; the single open\n151\tquestion is an internal topology decision handled by the Investigation and its\n152\tconditional branches. All onboarding work (E002–E005) is topology-independent and\n153\tdelivers risk-reduction value regardless of the outcome.\n154\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcf2380e6a315fa1","agent_id":"ab39adcea040bb08b","session_id":"c063278f-b757-405a-ad7d-6ea1f816e2d2","uuid":"4c351606-1c98-44d3-b963-dbc8becbd8fa","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:45:58.107Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae4f06bab97f4377","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
