{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2f32353719173ac","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-E006\n3\ttitle: Enable Feature Store as a managed component in the Platform Operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9006-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the topology investigation selects a different deployment\n16\t    topology than assumed, the operator reconciliation approach is rewritten to manage\n17\t    the other mechanism; the enablement capability itself remains.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Enable Feature Store as a managed component in the Platform Operator\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tMake the Feature Store (Feast) enableable through the Platform Operator like\n40\tany other managed RHOAI component: administrators toggle it on, the operator\n41\treconciles the selected deployment mechanism, and toggling it off removes it.\n42\tThe scope of the reconciliation follows the deployment topology decision —\n43\toperator-based deployment versus standalone server per project — which is why\n44\tthis epic is gated on that investigation.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Add the Feature Store to the Platform Operator's set of managed components\n49\t  with an administrator-facing enablement control, consistent with how other\n50\t  managed components are enabled.\n51\t- Implement reconciliation of the deployment mechanism selected by the\n52\t  topology decision: managing the operator-based deployment, or standing up\n53\t  the per-project server deployment.\n54\t- Reference the productized Feast artifacts by pinned image digest (the digest\n55\t  is a configuration reference filled in at execution time — the operator\n56\t  integration does not wait on the image builds by dependency).\n57\t- Expose the Feature Store enablement state in a form consistent with the\n58\t  operator's other managed components so the Dashboard can surface it.\n59\t- Support disabling: turning the Feature Store off removes what enabling\n60\t  created.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- Enabling the Feature Store through the Platform Operator results in a\n65\t  working deployment consistent with the selected topology.\n66\t- Disabling the Feature Store removes the deployed resources.\n67\t- The operator references pinned digests of the productized Feast images —\n68\t  no floating tags.\n69\t- The enablement state is exposed consistently with other managed components,\n70\t  in a form the Dashboard can read.\n71\t- Pinned image digests for the productized Feast artifacts are available at\n72\t  execution time (configuration gate, not a scheduling dependency).\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-1 (P0): administrators enable the supported Feature Store through the\n77\t  Platform Operator.\n78\t- HLR-3 (P1): produces the enablement surface the Dashboard displays.\n79\t\n80\t## Risks / Notes\n81\t\n82\t- Scope is gated on the deployment topology investigation; if the selected\n83\t  topology differs from the working assumption, this epic's reconciliation\n84\t  approach is rewritten (the enablement capability itself remains).\n85\t\n86\t## Open Questions\n87\t\n88\t- The deployment topology to reconcile is resolved by the gating\n89\t  investigation; no other open questions affect this epic's existence.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcf2380e6a315fa1","agent_id":"ab39adcea040bb08b","session_id":"c063278f-b757-405a-ad7d-6ea1f816e2d2","uuid":"86e1ba96-11ce-4240-9195-cb4fc470b30d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:46:20.691Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2f32353719173ac","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
