del selected by the topology decision (project-scoped servers or\n52\t  operator-managed endpoints).\n53\t- Gate the Feature Store presence on the component's enabled state, so it does\n54\t  not appear when the component is not enabled.\n55\t- No feature-authoring UI: links navigate out to the Feature Store endpoints.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- When the Feature Store is enabled, the Dashboard shows it as an enabled\n60\t  component.\n61\t- When the Feature Store is not enabled, the Dashboard does not show it.\n62\t- Users can reach the Feature Store endpoints for their project from the\n63\t  Dashboard via link-out.\n64\t- The integration follows the Dashboard's existing component feature-flag and\n65\t  configuration patterns.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-3 (P1): the Dashboard shows the Feature Store as an enabled component\n70\t  and links users to its endpoints per project.\n71\t\n72\t## Risks / Notes\n73\t\n74\t- The per-project endpoint shape is gated on the deployment topology\n75\t  investigation; if the selected topology differs from the working assumption,\n76\t  the endpoint-linking scope is rewritten (the enabled-component display\n77\t  remains).\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcf2380e6a315fa1","agent_id":"ab39adcea040bb08b","session_id":"c063278f-b757-405a-ad7d-6ea1f816e2d2","uuid":"f670f458-87ba-4d57-b31f-df2d355bfe16","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:46:26.543Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9da62872fe3a5ccb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
